.nh
.TH "GH-ISSUE-ARTIFACT-LIST" "1" "Oct 2026" "GitHub CLI 2.103.3" "GitHub CLI manual"

.SH NAME
gh-issue-artifact-list - List artifacts on an issue (preview)


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBgh issue artifact list {<issue-number> | <issue-url>} [flags]\fR


.SH DESCRIPTION
List the artifacts on an issue, in number order. Every artifact is listed
unless you set \fB--limit\fR\&.


.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB-q\fR, \fB--jq\fR \fB<expression>\fR
Filter JSON output using a jq expression

.TP
\fB--json\fR \fB<fields>\fR
Output JSON with the specified fields

.TP
\fB-L\fR, \fB--limit\fR \fB<int> (default 0)\fR
Maximum number of artifacts to fetch

.TP
\fB-t\fR, \fB--template\fR \fB<string>\fR
Format JSON output using a Go template; see "gh help formatting"

.TP
\fB--type\fR \fB<string>\fR
Filter by type: {generic|plan|link|embedded_html}


.SH OPTIONS INHERITED FROM PARENT COMMANDS
.TP
\fB-R\fR, \fB--repo\fR \fB<[HOST/]OWNER/REPO>\fR
Select another repository using the [HOST/]OWNER/REPO format


.SH ALIASES
gh issue artifact ls


.SH JSON FIELDS
\fBbody\fR, \fBbodyHtml\fR, \fBcreatedAt\fR, \fBcreator\fR, \fBdescription\fR, \fBid\fR, \fBname\fR, \fBnumber\fR, \fBtype\fR, \fBupdatedAt\fR, \fBupdatedByActor\fR, \fBurl\fR


.SH EXIT CODES
0: Successful execution

.PP
1: Error

.PP
2: Command canceled

.PP
4: Authentication required

.PP
NOTE: Specific commands may have additional exit codes. Refer to the command's help for more information.


.SH EXAMPLE
.EX
# List the artifacts on issue 142
$ gh issue artifact list 142

# List only links
$ gh issue artifact list 142 --type link

# Print artifact numbers and names as JSON
$ gh issue artifact list 142 --json number,name

.EE


.SH SEE ALSO
\fBgh-issue-artifact(1)\fR
